      "body": "Strategy is to work at a startup who have raised money from investors. It shows they \"might\" have a great product. You might get less equity though, but considering 80-95% of startups would fail over the lifetime, it might be worth the less equity in my opinion. \n\nAnother strategy would be to get a remote job at big tech and a remote job at a startup. You could improve your skills and career growth a lot while also benefitting from compensations, but you're mostly likely going to throw away your work-life balance working at two jobs. ",
